@feat-spl-003 @sovereign-planning-loop @assumption-dialogue
Feature: Assumption Dialogue
  As James, an identity-pinned planning originator
  I want the factory's proposed planning assumptions delivered to my Slack
  thread as individually decidable items, and every planning update from the
  factory to reach me in that same thread
  So that a planning run's assumptions get real per-item human judgment
  (never a rubber stamp), the decisions become durable curation signal for
  the learning flywheel, and no planning message to a human ever evaporates
  unread

  Background:
    Given Jarvis is running with a connected NATS transport
    And the Slack Socket Mode connection is established
    And the planning notification consumer is running
    And Rich is configured as an authorized approval operator
    And a planning run originated by James exists with its originating Slack thread known to the factory

  # ─── GROUP A: Key Examples ──────────────────────────────────────────────

  # Why: The feature's first deliverable — today Mode P's messages to the human
  # expire unread (no consumer; JARVIS stream retains 1h/1000). This is the
  # missing return channel, gate criterion for the WS1 §5 session.
  @key-example @smoke @task:TASK-SPL003-J01
  Scenario: A planned handoff notification is rendered into the originating thread
    Given the planning run has reached its planned handoff
    When forge publishes a planning notification announcing the handoff
    Then the notification should be posted as a reply in the thread of James's original message
    And the notification should include the handoff message verbatim
    And the notification should include the correlation identifier of the planning run
    And no notification should be posted outside that thread

  # Why: The core dialogue surface — one item per assumption, forced per-item
  # decisions; the anti-rubber-stamp UX is load-bearing for WS4 preference pairs.
  @key-example @smoke @task:TASK-SPL003-J02
  Scenario: A planning checkpoint renders as a per-assumption decision prompt
    Given forge pauses the planning run at the assumption checkpoint
    When Jarvis receives the planning approval request
    Then a decision prompt should be posted in the originating thread
    And every proposed assumption should appear as its own decision item
    And each item should display the assumption text and its confidence tag
    # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] ASSUM-005 — the edit choice opens a prefilled input for a replacement value
    And each item should offer exactly three choices: approve, edit, and defer
    And no control should be offered that decides more than one assumption at once

  # Why: The approve disposition path — distinct per-item dispositions in the
  # published decision are the WS4 curation signal (harvest: 0 'considered').
  @key-example @smoke @task:TASK-SPL003-J03a
  Scenario: Approving every assumption publishes one decision carrying per-item dispositions
    Given a decision prompt with three proposed assumptions is displayed
    When Rich approves each assumption one by one
    # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] ASSUM-010 — the decision publishes when the final undecided item is decided
    Then exactly one decision should be published for the checkpoint
    # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] ASSUM-003 — dispositions ride the frozen approval response contract
    And the decision should record a confirmed disposition for each assumption distinctly
    And each disposition should record Rich's member id as the decider
    And the planning run should be able to proceed

  # Why: The edit disposition path — an overridden value is the highest-value
  # curation signal and the input to the forge revision cycle.
  @key-example @task:TASK-SPL003-J03b
  Scenario: Editing an assumption records an overridden disposition carrying the replacement
    Given a decision prompt with three proposed assumptions is displayed
    When Rich chooses edit on one assumption and provides a corrected value
    Then that assumption's disposition should be recorded as overridden with the corrected value
    And the dispositions of the other assumptions should be unaffected

  # Why: The defer disposition path — defer is a real disposition, not a dropped
  # signal; it drives another dialogue cycle on the forge side.
  @key-example @task:TASK-SPL003-J03a
  Scenario: Deferring an assumption records a deferred disposition and asks for another cycle
    Given a decision prompt with three proposed assumptions is displayed
    When Rich defers one assumption and approves the others
    Then that assumption's disposition should be recorded as deferred
    And the published decision should ask the planning run for another dialogue cycle
    And the other assumptions' dispositions should be preserved in the published decision

  # Why: Dialogue continuity — revision cycles stay in the one conversation the
  # originator is watching, with the cycle number visible.
  @key-example @task:TASK-SPL003-J02
  Scenario: A revision cycle re-renders in the same originating thread with its cycle number
    Given a first dialogue cycle completed with one assumption overridden
    When forge publishes the revised checkpoint for the next cycle
    Then the new decision prompt should be posted in the same originating thread
    And the prompt should show which dialogue cycle it belongs to

  # Why: The WS4 join — dispositions must be recoverable from the durable trace,
  # keyed by assumption, or preference pairs cannot be built.
  @key-example @task:TASK-SPL003-J03a
  Scenario: Per-assumption dispositions land in the planning trace record
    Given a decision prompt has been fully decided with a mix of approvals and one edit
    When the decision is published
    Then the published decision should carry every disposition keyed by its assumption identifier
    And the planning run's durable trace record should preserve each disposition distinctly

  # ─── GROUP B: Boundary Conditions ───────────────────────────────────────

